[#:seon.task{:name "hosting-an-agent-costs-seconds-and-a-hundred-megabytes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "On a fresh disposable root, hosting an MCP agent (host/host! on a new :agent-* branch) plus its first SCI run took ~1.4-1.6 s and kept ~100 MB of live heap per agent, over the 1 s / 10 MB budget. Cause: a new branch connection builds its own index tree; its first whole-program reads (seon.sci.eval/load-core-namespaces! in every acquisition, then the first form's analysis) restored ~3,400 index nodes from disk because the store's shared node cache held Datahike's default 1,000 nodes, so each branch decompressed them again (1.2 GB allocated) and its tree kept a private copy. Correct: a new branch reuses the nodes the store already holds and acquisition loads namespaces only when it derives a base. Proof: a second hosted branch restores no index node from storage."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.store/datahike-configuration seon.sci.eval/acquire!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/host-cost/host-cost-notes.md"}}]
